issue-001 done. Now issue-002.

Add JoinSlug:
```go
// JoinSlug 把多个片段各自 slug 后以 "/" 连接。
// 空白片段会被跳过。
func JoinSlug(parts ...string) string {
	slugs := make([]string, 0, len(parts))
	for _, p := range parts {
		if s := Slug(p); s != "" {
			slugs = append(slugs, s)
		}
	}
	return strings.Join(slugs, "/")
}
```

Test:
```go
func TestJoinSlug(t *testing.T) {
	if got := JoinSlug("Hello World", "Big Day"); got != "hello-world/big-day" {
		t.Fatalf("JoinSlug(...) = %q", got)
	}
	if got := JoinSlug("a", "", "b"); got != "a/b" {
		t.Fatalf("JoinSlug(...) = %q", got)
	}
}
```

Also test pure whitespace skipped? Acceptance says "空串与纯空白被跳过". The second case only tests "". Let me include a whitespace-only part too to actually cover the stated acceptance. E.g. `JoinSlug("a", "   ", "b")` → "a/b". I'll add that. Keep minimal but it's an explicit acceptance condition ("纯空白"). I'll test both empty and whitespace.

Actually the acceptance example uses `JoinSlug("a", "", "b")`. The prose says "空串与纯空白被跳过". So testing whitespace too is justified.

